    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OUaQTzCWQalf"
      },
      "source": [
        "Since the data is not balanced using SMOTE to balace the data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6n74vsoqQoxS"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Generate Synthetic dataset to balnce the dataset**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VPirUi0hQ1Nm"
      },
      "source": [
        "Using SMOTE for this task\n",
        "genreating synthetic sample for class 0 (thats why using minority)\n",
        "if used auto then all the classes have same number of data which can drop the accuracy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yPLhaUBeHXrj"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "smote = SMOTE(sampling_strategy='minority')\n",
        "X, y = smote.fit_resample(X, y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sSDTZOFiRWNc"
      },
      "source": [
        "### **Now splitting the datasert into training and testing set**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "85xeJhSu7q8J"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size = 0.2, random_state = 43)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "XsauZxqfSS9b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## **Creating the model**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Nk-bBrkeSiOq"
      },
      "source": [
        "building an RNN for this"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MdJjQolH5t0i"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "dimension = 50 #features and factors on which we prioratize eevery word\n",
        "\n",
        "model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "    #embedding layer\n",
        "    keras.layers.Embedding(vocab_size, dimension, input_length = sentence_length),\n",
        "    # LSTM layer\n",
        "    keras.layers.LSTM(100,return_sequences=True),\n",
        "    keras.layers.LSTM(50, return_sequences=True),\n",
        "    keras.layers.LSTM(50),\n",
        "    #output layer\n",
        "    keras.layers.Dense(3, activation = 'softmax')\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "#best optimizer is adam\n",
        "model.compile(optimizer = 'adam',\n",
        "              loss = 'sparse_categorical_crossentropy',\n",
        "              metrics = ['accuracy'])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wZ2dxKJi7I-u"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model.summary()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "x7i-2OM37Kka",
        "outputId": "75320270-a53c-40a3-9e67-65dd0fa88cc6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train, epochs = 10, batch_size=32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
